WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.434
-I gotta say, we did "Password"
together,

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:04.567
and it was the most fun
I ever had.

00:00:04.567 --> 00:00:06.601
I loved working with you
so much.

00:00:06.601 --> 00:00:07.601
August 9th --
-August 9th.

00:00:07.601 --> 00:00:09.567
-Tuesday nights,
in three weeks from now.

00:00:09.567 --> 00:00:11.868
Just set your DVRs,
watch it with everyone.

00:00:11.868 --> 00:00:14.067
It's a good --
We had so much fun.

00:00:14.067 --> 00:00:15.567
We had great celebs come on.

00:00:15.567 --> 00:00:17.901
-Oh, yes, Meghan Trainor --
-Meghan Trainor was good.

00:00:17.901 --> 00:00:18.901
-She was a lot of fun.

00:00:18.901 --> 00:00:20.200
-She was a little rusty
at first.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:21.901
-Yeah, yeah, she was like --
but then she got into it,

00:00:21.901 --> 00:00:23.133
and we're like,
"Okay, miss girl."

00:00:23.133 --> 00:00:25.534
-Yeah, then she started
crushing it, yeah.

00:00:25.534 --> 00:00:26.868
Martin Short made me laugh.

00:00:26.868 --> 00:00:29.467
-Oh, my gosh, he was making me
laugh the entire time.

00:00:29.467 --> 00:00:31.801
He's so funny.
-Ridiculous. He came out.

00:00:31.801 --> 00:00:32.968
Jon Hamm I think
is the first episode.

00:00:32.968 --> 00:00:34.567
-Oh, Jon Hamm, yeah,
he's so cool.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:36.667
-Yeah. And he's like, yeah,
he's in the biggest movie ever.

00:00:36.667 --> 00:00:38.033
It's like no big deal.

00:00:38.033 --> 00:00:39.601
Speaking of being
in the biggest movie,

00:00:39.601 --> 00:00:40.534
I want to talk about "Nope."

00:00:40.534 --> 00:00:42.067
-Ooh!
-Yeah!

00:00:42.067 --> 00:00:43.133
I mean, that's what
I want to talk about.

00:00:43.133 --> 00:00:44.968
[ Cheers and applause ]
-I'm so excited!

00:00:44.968 --> 00:00:46.467
-It's out.
-I know. I know.

00:00:46.467 --> 00:00:49.734
-It's a big deal.
This Friday -- IMAX, everything.

00:00:49.734 --> 00:00:51.767
You crush it when you --
when you do all the --

00:00:51.767 --> 00:00:53.901
Did you know Jordan Peele
before you did this movie?

00:00:53.901 --> 00:00:57.534
-So, I did a "Key and Peele"
sketch with him when I was 17.

00:00:57.534 --> 00:00:59.100
And then I -- Yeah, we didn't --

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:01.100
we never did anything else
after that.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:02.234
-What sketch was it?
Do I remember it?

00:01:02.234 --> 00:01:04.667
-So, I played Malia Obama's
translator.

00:01:04.667 --> 00:01:06.367
Remember he used to do
the translator sketches?

00:01:06.367 --> 00:01:08.567
-Oh, the angry translator?
-Yeah, so I was angry.

00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:11.501
I was, like, real sassy,
Malia Obama ready to get up out.

00:01:11.501 --> 00:01:13.934
[ Laughter ]
-That's funny.

00:01:13.934 --> 00:01:16.200
-But, yeah, that was quick
and it was funny.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:17.834
He was so nice.
And that was kind of like,

00:01:17.834 --> 00:01:20.934
the first time I had really been
like, "Okay, I'm doing comedy."

00:01:20.934 --> 00:01:22.834
Like, I had done sitcoms before.
-Yeah.

00:01:22.834 --> 00:01:24.200
-But I was like,
"Okay, I'm into sketch."

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:26.133
So I really -- I do owe it to
Jordan to get me in there

00:01:26.133 --> 00:01:27.601
'cause now I do it all the time.

00:01:27.601 --> 00:01:30.267
-Yeah, and, by the way,
you do so much stuff.

00:01:30.267 --> 00:01:31.934
You're a great follow on the
socials, by the way, I will say.

00:01:31.934 --> 00:01:34.434
-Aw, thanks.
-I saw you did something recent

00:01:34.434 --> 00:01:36.501
with Vice President
Kamala Harris.

00:01:36.501 --> 00:01:37.901
-Oh, yes!

00:01:37.901 --> 00:01:39.901
[ Cheers and applause ]
The V.P.

00:01:39.901 --> 00:01:41.367
-Wait.

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:44.601
Now, do you get nervous
when you --

00:01:44.601 --> 00:01:46.100
This was a couple weeks ago.

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:48.200
-I mean, it is nerve-wracking
but just because I want to make

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:49.601
sure, that, you know,
"Okay, I'm doing my best."

00:01:49.601 --> 00:01:51.100
You know what I mean?
The Secret Service was there.

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:52.367
I was like, "How y'all doin'?"

00:01:52.367 --> 00:01:54.100
I wanted to make sure that I was
like, "I'm professional.

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:55.534
Yeah, I'm not gonna hurt
the V.P."

00:01:55.534 --> 00:01:57.000
-No, you're very professional,
yeah.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.400
But you made her laugh by doing
an impression of her.

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:03.434
-Oh, my gosh. Her meme is my
favorite -- "We did it, Joe."

00:02:03.434 --> 00:02:05.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.267 --> 00:02:07.801
"You're the President of
the United States of America."

00:02:07.801 --> 00:02:11.133
I love it! I had to tell her,
because I'm like, "Girl!

00:02:11.133 --> 00:02:12.868
That meme -- "We did it, Joe."

00:02:12.868 --> 00:02:15.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:17.367
-Speaking of vice presidents,
by the way,

00:02:17.367 --> 00:02:19.834
a few years ago you did this
thing for --

00:02:19.834 --> 00:02:22.300
I think it's a "Vanity Fair"
thing.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:23.868
A lie detector test.
-Oh!

00:02:23.868 --> 00:02:26.667
-And they showed you a photo of
Vice President Dick Cheney.

00:02:26.667 --> 00:02:28.767
-[ Laughs ]
-And you did not recognize him.

00:02:28.767 --> 00:02:31.834
And your reaction became
an instant meme.

00:02:31.834 --> 00:02:33.267
We have a clip of this.
-Yes.

00:02:33.267 --> 00:02:35.067
-Let's take a look.

00:02:35.067 --> 00:02:37.133
-Who the hell is...

00:02:37.133 --> 00:02:40.767
Ooh, y'all are really testing me
on some stuff that I --

00:02:40.767 --> 00:02:43.167
I hate to say it. I hope I don't
sound ridiculous.

00:02:43.167 --> 00:02:44.501
I don't know who this man is.

00:02:44.501 --> 00:02:46.133
[ Laughter ]
I mean, he could be walking down

00:02:46.133 --> 00:02:49.000
the street, I wouldn't --
I wouldn't know a thing.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:50.634
Sorry to this man.

00:02:50.634 --> 00:02:52.467
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:52.467 --> 00:02:55.834
-"Sorry to this man"
was everywhere.

00:02:55.834 --> 00:02:59.434
-Yeah, that -- I don't know what
is going on.

00:02:59.434 --> 00:03:01.567
The Internet is so funny
interesting to me

00:03:01.567 --> 00:03:03.434
because how would I --
I had no idea --

00:03:03.434 --> 00:03:04.968
I really was just sorry
to the man

00:03:04.968 --> 00:03:08.133
because I knew that I didn't
know something.

00:03:08.133 --> 00:03:09.267
You know what I mean?

00:03:09.267 --> 00:03:10.701
-Do people say that to you
on the street?

00:03:10.701 --> 00:03:13.167
-All the time. That was like
I had a hit movie in theaters.

00:03:13.167 --> 00:03:15.834
I was in "Jaws"
when that came out.

00:03:15.834 --> 00:03:17.400
Crazy.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:19.834
"Sorry to that man."
-"Sorry to this man," you know?

00:03:19.834 --> 00:03:21.601
[ Laughter ]
Crazy.

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:24.400
-I mean, "Nope" is, I think,

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:26.434
going to be one of the biggest
movies out there.

00:03:26.434 --> 00:03:28.701
I cannot wait for this.
I don't know anything about it.

00:03:28.701 --> 00:03:30.901
I'm scared. Is it gonna scare
me? Am I scared?

00:03:30.901 --> 00:03:32.133
-So there's a lot going on.

00:03:32.133 --> 00:03:33.767
You're definitely gonna have
some spooky vibes.

00:03:33.767 --> 00:03:36.801
But, you know, what Jordan does
with his films is, the horror

00:03:36.801 --> 00:03:38.400
that he puts in the film is
really a metaphor

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:39.901
for the horrors of the world.
-Yep.

00:03:39.901 --> 00:03:41.400
-So I think you'll really relate
to it.

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:43.934
A lot of things about, you know,
a spectacle,

00:03:43.934 --> 00:03:47.200
exploitation,
our obsession with attention.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:48.734
It's a lot of different stuff,
a lot of nuggets

00:03:48.734 --> 00:03:50.000
that you're gonna keep
pulling back.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.334
-I think this is the year of
Keke Palmer, by the way.

00:03:52.334 --> 00:03:53.534
I'm just gonna say it right now.
-Aw.

00:03:53.534 --> 00:03:55.667
-You are unbelievable.
-Aw, stop.

00:03:55.667 --> 00:03:57.934
-And well deserved.
You work your butt off.

00:03:57.934 --> 00:03:59.801
You're so good.
I wanna show everyone a clip.

00:03:59.801 --> 00:04:02.367
Here's my favorite Keke Palmer
in "Nope."

00:04:02.367 --> 00:04:03.801
-Ooh.
-Take a look.

00:04:03.801 --> 00:04:05.834
-You set it up the right way.

00:04:05.834 --> 00:04:08.501
Man, I'm talking rich and famous
for life.

00:04:08.501 --> 00:04:10.267
How you doing? You look pretty.

00:04:10.267 --> 00:04:12.133
Looks like she got a big house.
-How?

00:04:12.133 --> 00:04:13.734
-"How" what? How we put it out?
-Mm.

00:04:13.734 --> 00:04:15.000
-But that's what I'm saying.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:16.734
We don't just go for
the quick cash, okay?

00:04:16.734 --> 00:04:19.334
We go to a credible platform
to do the story.

00:04:19.334 --> 00:04:20.968
-What's that, like "Oprah"?
-Yeah.

00:04:20.968 --> 00:04:23.501
Like "Oprah," for example.
After that, everybody want in.

00:04:23.501 --> 00:04:25.868
-But I'm saying, there's plenty
of videos...online.

00:04:25.868 --> 00:04:27.701
I saw one the other day
that wasn't on "Oprah."

00:04:27.701 --> 00:04:29.400
-I didn't say "Oprah,"
you said "Oprah."

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:30.901
You love "Oprah."

00:04:30.901 --> 00:04:33.300
Look, all I'm saying is all
that...online is fake.

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:35.868
Low quality. Ain't nobody going
to get what we gonna get.

00:04:35.868 --> 00:04:37.501
-What we gonna get?
-The shot.

00:04:37.501 --> 00:04:39.567
-What shot?
-The shot.

00:04:39.567 --> 00:04:42.334
The money shot. Undeniable.
Singular.

00:04:42.334 --> 00:04:44.667
The "Oprah" shot.

00:04:44.667 --> 00:04:46.400
-The "Oprah" shot?

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:49.901
-That's right!
You gotta get the "Oprah" shot!

00:04:49.901 --> 00:04:51.167
Keke Palmer, everybody.

00:04:51.167 --> 00:04:55.000
"Nope" is in theaters and IMAX
this Friday.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:57.934
Catch "Password" August 9th
at 10:00 p.m.

00:04:57.934 --> 00:04:59.801
on NBC after
"America's Got Talent."

